      <memberdef kind="function" id="group__network__getters_1ga902f41cfcc000cf54f3b8cd29b799014" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>const int</type>
        <definition>const int ndxlGetNetworkChannels</definition>
        <argsstring>(NDXLNetwork *_Network, NDXLChannel **_Channels)</argsstring>
        <name>ndxlGetNetworkChannels</name>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="group__ndxl__objects_1gaefd105209efdd9f61bea4c3f76770d37" kindref="member">NDXLNetwork</ref> *</type>
          <declname>_Network</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="ndxlcore_8h_1a40b73c1a687ab1376515b42d4294c079" kindref="member">NDXLChannel</ref> **</type>
          <declname>_Channels</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Gets a list of all the noise channels in a network. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">_Network</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Target network to retrieve the noise channels of.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="out">_Channels</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Pointer to a user-allocated array of <ref refid="ndxlcore_8h_1a40b73c1a687ab1376515b42d4294c079" kindref="member">NDXLChannel</ref> pointers. The array must contain at least ndxlGetNetworkChannelCount(_Network) elements. The function populates the array in-place.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>If either _Network or _Channels are NULL, returns <ref refid="group__ndxl__err_1gae9261a8e1c9a6cebdc947ee5798cca1e" kindref="member">NDXL_ERR</ref>, otherwise populates _Channels with the noise channel pointers associated with _Network, and returns NDXL_OK.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>The caller retains ownership of the array, but not of the <ref refid="ndxlcore_8h_1a40b73c1a687ab1376515b42d4294c079" kindref="member">NDXLChannel</ref> objects referenced by its elements. These pointers refer to the original objects in the network, so modifications through them affect those objects directly. The returned list can be used to modify or destroy its referenced objects without invalidating the array itself.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="warning"><para>The function does not verify the capacity of the supplied array. Providing an inadequately sized array can result in out-of-bounds writes and undefined behaviour.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="par"><title>Errors raised</title><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><ref refid="group__ndxl__err_1gaf6b8bdcb87bdd7944810152b510101e4" kindref="member">NDXL_ARG_ERR</ref> : _Network is NULL.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><ref refid="group__ndxl__err_1gaf6b8bdcb87bdd7944810152b510101e4" kindref="member">NDXL_ARG_ERR</ref> : _Channels is NULL.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="group__network__getters_1gaf406de51649554e4d14851554f85572b" kindref="member">ndxlGetNetworkChannelCount</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
